           DIGITAL COMPLETES SALE OF STORAGE HEADS, DISK
            AND TAPES BUSINESSES TO QUANTUM CORPORATION


    Digital's Storage Business Unit Experiences Continued Growth
                     with StorageWorks Products


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 3, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the completion of the sale of Digital's magnetic 
disk drive, tape drive, solid state disk, and thin-film heads 
businesses to Quantum Corporation for $360 million, $70 million of 
which is to be paid in the form of a 6-month interest-bearing note.  
The purchase price is subject to adjustments in accordance with the 
purchase agreement.  The transaction, which was announced by both 
companies on July 19, also includes Digital's 81% interest in Rocky 
Mountain Magnetics, Inc., a key developer of magneto-resistive heads 
technology. 

     The sale includes a supply agreement in which Quantum will 
supply a significant percentage of Digital's hard disk drive, 
solid state disk drive, and tape drive requirements for its 
StorageWorks subsystems and core computer systems businesses. 

     Digital's Storage Business Unit remains within the corporation, 
with the continued growth of storage subsystems sales of 
StorageWorks products for multiple client/server computing 
platforms, including Digital, Novell, Sun, and UNIX environments. 
Further, Digital's Video and Interactive Information Services 
business, a leader in the delivery of end-to-end interactive video 
solutions, also remains as a strategic business for the corporation. 

     Approximately 5,000 regular and temporary employees are joining
Quantum from Digital. In addition, under the terms of the sale 
agreement, Digital has sold Quantum facilities in Shrewsbury, 
Massachusetts, and Penang, Malaysia, and leased facilities in 
Colorado Springs, Colorado, and Batam, Indonesia. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP
platforms, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.  
