UNIX commercial computing power yet," said John O'Keefe, vice 
president of UNIX Systems Marketing for Digital. "The range of 
applications and capabilities, along with the relationships we are 
announcing with our business partners, place us in the forefront in 
solving customers' business problems for the rest of the century."

     DEC OSF/1 software, Digital's implementation of the UNIX 
operating system, is the cornerstone of the company's strategy for 
meeting customer demand for an industry standard UNIX. A 
just-conducted study shows that DEC OSF/1 V3.0 leads the industry by 
providing 97.5 per cent of the APIs called for in the final issue of 
SPEC 1170 from X/Open, the specification which will define UNIX. 
SPEC 1170 is being incorporated into an updated version of the XPG4 
standard to be knows as XPG4v2. Digital plans to include its runtime 
implementation of the Open Software Foundation's Distributed 
Computing Environment (DCE) in its next release of the operating 
system, further enhancing the delivery of standards for customers.

     Digital is a major sponsor of the E-MAIL Village Green, part of 
the Internet Village. The E-MAIL Village Green lets UNIX Expo 
attendees have access to hands-on E-MAIL. The Internet Village is a 
showcase designed to inform conference attendees of the power and 
flexibility of the Internet in delivering information on a worldwide 
basis.  Digital is a leader in providing systems, software, and 
services to users of the Internet.

     o 	HIGH AVAILABILITY  -- AdvantageCluster Systems -- Digital is
