               DIGITAL ENHANCES HUBwatch FOR WINDOWS,
              BRINGING FULL-FUNCTION NETWORK MANAGEMENT
                   CAPABILITIES TO THE PC PLATFORM


 HUBwatch for Windows Offered in Low-Cost, Managed Stackable Package


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 3, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today introduced a new version of HUBwatch for Windows that 
significantly extends the network management power of PC platforms 
by providing the ability to create virtual LANs and manage Ethernet 
and FDDI switched LANs from a PC.  At $495, HUBwatch is the lowest 
cost, full-function hub management application on the market today.  
HUBwatch can either run standalone from a 386/486 Windows PC or be 
launched from popular enterprise managers, such as HP OpenView for 
Windows.  Digital is bringing its easy-to-use HUBwatch management 
and industry-leading pricing to workgroup environments in a new 
stackable package called the Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack.  At 
only $100 per port, this new package, which provides 24 ports of 
Ethernet connectivity, is the industry's lowest cost managed 
stackable offering.

     The introduction of switching into LANs has boosted the network 
manager's ability to create flexible workgroups, know as virtual 
LANs, based on traffic patterns, security requirements or 
prioritization concerns.  Network management must keep pace with the 
growing complexity of networks, by covering a broad range of network 
devices and technologies and providing flexible, easy-to-use
functionality. 

     According to William Maro, Digital's vice president, Network 
Product Marketing and Engineering, "Network management is evolving 
from simple port level monitoring to the management of high 
performance switched networks and virtual LANs.  Digital is 
delivering on its strategy to provide easy access to the full power
of Digital's network products on a low-cost PC platform."

     John McConnell, president of McConnell Consulting added, 
"Digital offers the unique combination of a strong management tool 
on a Windows PC with links to enterprise management platforms.  
HUBwatch provides integrated management of hubs, switches, FDDI and 
virtual LANs through its graphical user interface.  Network managers 
can work with an inexpensive, familiar PC without sacrificing access 
to UNIX platform services."

HUBwatch for Windows: Full Function Management from a PC 

     HUBwatch for Windows offers comprehensive management of 
Digital's SNMP-based network hardware products, using the familiar 
Windows-based graphical user interface. The new version of HUBwatch 
manages all DEChub modules including Digital's recently-announced 
Ethernet and FDDI switches--the PEswitch 900TX, providing desktop 
Ethernet to FDDI, and the DECswitch 900EE and DECswitch 900EF, 
providing interLAN departmental switching. 

     Digital has simplified the difficult job of building and 
managing virtual LANs. Digital's HUBwatch for Windows uses an 
intuitive and graphical approach, allowing network managers to draw 
LAN configurations using any LAN technology in any configuration.  
The result is a pictorial method of creating virtual LANs, which
then can be modified easily as workgroup needs change, technologies 
are added, or traffic increases.  

     The built-in intelligence of the HUBwatch for Windows software 
allows both central network managers as well as workgroup-based LAN 
administrators to handle the complexity of building a virtual LAN 
and take full advantage of the power of switched networks.

     Jim Hutchinson of Boston's Children's Hospital noted, "Digital 
provides a very low cost, high-function, easy-to-use management 
solution that can connect, manage and integrate our diverse LANs 
with a lot less resources than approaches we've tried in the past."

The Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack:  An Intelligent Stackable Solution

     For customers requiring a managed Ethernet solution, Digital 
has integrated HUBwatch for Windows into an intelligent stackable 
network package, the Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack.  This new 
package offers 24 managed ports with the option to expand to 56 
ports or to add remote access, bridging, routing or wireless
capabilities.  The Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack is a flexible 
building block that can be used in small PC LANs as well as complex 
enterprise networks.

     "Our distributor and reseller partners are enthusiastic about 
offering the Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack." Digital's Maro adds. 
"Customers receive a total network solution with an easy-to-order 
and install package at a very attractive price.  In addition, by 
providing the same point and click interface and the same management 
functionality either in-band or out-of-band, we've given network 
managers and VARs who manage customer LANs an easy, cost-effective 
way to manage remote LANs."

     At $2490, the Managed DEChub 90 Starter-Pack delivers unmatched 
stackable network management value.  It includes three eight-port 
DECrepeater 90T units, one-eight-slot DEChub 90 backplane and power 
supply, HUBwatch for Windows and the DECagent 90 management module.

     For customers that need 'basic' connectivity without 
management, Digital continues to offer a DEChub 90 Starter-Pack for 
$1,995, with three eight-port DECrepeater 90T units and one 
eight-slot DEChub 90 backplane and power supply.

Pricing and Availability

     The DEChub 90 Starter-Packs are available today and will be 
offered through December 31, 1994.

     HUBwatch for Windows is also available today for $495.  Digital 
offers other versions of HUBwatch on OSF/1 and OpenVMS platforms.

     Digital, a leading provider of stackable network solutions, 
continues to be a significant contributor to the development of many 
popular networking technologies including Ethernet, FDDI and ATM 
LANs, network switches, routers, bridges and terminal servers.  
Digital has networked more than 10 million users worldwide.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
                                ####

