            DIGITAL STEALS SHOW IN 1994 "HOT IRON" AWARDS


NEW YORK, NY -- October 4, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
took top honors today in AIM Technology's 1994 Hot Iron Awards for 
UNIX Computer Systems, announced here at UNIX EXPO. Digital received 
ten of the sixteen awards for its workstation and server products.

     The Digital systems honored today include workstations and 
servers based on Digital's 64-bit RISC-based Alpha AXP 
microprocessor, and Digital's premier Personal Computer servers. 

     "These results demonstrate the sweeping advantages Digital's 
UNIX-based Alpha AXP systems provide customers today," said John 
O'Keefe, Digital's vice president, UNIX Systems Marketing. "The 
combination of DEC OSF/1, the world's most standards-compliant UNIX 
operating system, and Digital's Alpha AXP systems family gives users 
the pure 64-bit performance, future scalability and economy they 
expect for their compute-intensive applications." 		    

     "There have been a lot of claims made lately in the PC server 
