           SYSTEM HEALTHCHECK FOR NOVELL NETWARE AND SUNOS
         PROVIDES ECONOMICAL, COMPREHENSIVE SYSTEM ANALYSIS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 12, 1994 -- Novell NETWare and SunOS 
customers can now optimize the performance of their systems and 
networks by using System Healthcheck from Digital Equipment 
Corporation.  System Healthcheck is an economical, comprehensive 
data analysis service that provides users with detailed reports and 
recommendations for optimizing system performance as well as 
performing preventive maintenance measures and ensuring overall 
system and network health.

     With that information, an enterprise can optimize the 
performance of its systems, making the most of its technology 
investment.

     System Healthcheck measures network configuration, system and 
disk performance, system security and file usage against more than 
400 standard criteria simultaneously, eliminating the risk of false 
data comparisons, so an enterprise can optimize its systems' 
performance and identify existing or potential problems.  Until now, 
achieving the same level of comprehensive systems testing required 
multiple tools from multiple vendors -- a difficult and expensive 
alternative.

     "This service offers IS managers the ability to audit and 
benchmark their systems to obtain objective and documented system 
performance.  With this information, IS managers can now identify 
system productivity problems and the need for system changes," said 
John Rando, vice president, Multivendor Customer Services.

     "Offering System Healthcheck for users of Novell NETWare and 
SunOS demonstrates Digital's commitment to delivering system 
management capabilities into multivendor environments," added Rando. 
"We will continue to offer our customers superior assessment tools 
in the future for multivendor environments worldwide.  

     Because System Healthcheck captures performance data while the 
system is operating, it eliminates the need for a costly system 
shutdown.  In addition, IS managers can choose the data collection 
method that best meets their needs:  System Healthcheck can collect 
data on a set of disks that can be run at the IS department's 
convenience; onsite by a Digital specialist; or offsite, by remote 
link.

     Once the data is collected, analysis is performed at Digital 
using the company's expert system-based software.  The results are 
developed in a System Healthcheck Assessment Report, which 
summarizes the findings, weighs and prioritizes conditions that 
require further diagnosis or immediate resolution, and recommends a 
targeted solution.

     The service includes a follow-up consultation with a Digital 
specialist to discuss the findings and to assist in planning 
recommended action.  The price is determined by the data collection 
method and level of consultation.  For instance, System Healthcheck 
collected remotely or on disks by the customer with a telephone 
consultation is US$700.  

A similar system management assessment delivered traditionally by a 
consultant could cost over US$10,000, depending on the size of the 
configuration.

     System Healthcheck also is available on OpenVMS (VAX and Alpha 
AXP) and ULTRIX (VAX and RISC), and is sold direct, as well as by 
Digital's channel partners.

     System Healthcheck is one of a comprehensive range of services 
offered by Digital's Multivendor Customer Services.  MCS provides 
system support and service for more than 14,000 hardware and 
software products worldwide.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global markets.
