                        Background For Editors
    
    
            System Healthcheck for Novell NETWare and SunOS
                  From Digital Equipment Corporation
    
    
     Just as people should have periodic health checkups to uncover 
potential problems, so should computer systems. Today's multivendor 
computing environments create the potential for hidden problems and 
their associated costs for any size enterprise. The solution is to 
diagnose and solve problems before they occur, not wait until they 
affect system performance.
   
     Digital's solution is System Healthcheck, a unified system
management assessment service that captures a system's performance data
while it's operating, comparing all areas of system operation against
more than 400 standard criteria. Results are analyzed based on the
performance benchmarks of a similarly configured, fully optimized
system, with potential and actual problems identified and prioritized
for resolution. In addition, System Healthcheck includes a follow-up 
consultation with a Digital specialist to answer any questions or 
assist you in making system setting adjustments.
  
     System Healthcheck is available for users of Novell NETWare and
SunOS. It is a fast, cost-effective way of optimizing performance by
examining all major system management aspects of your computing
environment including system configuration, system operations, system
security, file usage and system performance and availability.
  
     System Healthcheck is flexibly packaged. It is currently available 
three ways: first, onsite with a packaged set of disks, allowing IS 
managers to collect the data on their systems at their convenience; 
second, the data collection also can be conducted onsite by a Digital 
specialist; or third, Digital, via remote access using a secure link, 
can capture the appropriate data when authorized.
  
     Once the data is collected, it is analyzed at Digital using the 
company's expert system-based software. Results are compiled in a 
System Healthcheck Assessment Report that summarizes findings, weighs 
and prioritizes conditions requiring further diagnosis or immediate 
resolution, and recommends a suitable course of action.
  
     The service also includes a follow-up consultation with a Digital 
specialist to discuss the report findings and to assist in planning 
recommended actions.
  
     System Healthcheck is a worldwide service offering. Reports
generated are available in multiple languages.
  
