              DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW RAID CONTROLLER AND
       HIGH-AVAILABILITY STORAGE ENCLOSURE AND SHELF FOR OEMS


    StorageWorks SC-4600 RAID Controller and HA Series of Storage
         Units Offer Reliability and Performance Needed For
                   Critical Business Applications


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 12, 1994 -- Digital Equipment today 
expanded its portfolio of StorageWorks solutions for OEMs with a new 
SCSI RAID controller, a new modular subsystems enclosure and a shelf 
unit.  The SC-4600 RAID controller offers industry-leading 
performance and battery backed-up read/write cache.  In the event of 
a power failure, the battery backed-up cache will maintain cache 
data for a minimum of 100 hours, preventing loss of critical data.  
The SC-4600 is compatible with the new StorageWorks HA-2400C high-
availability enclosure, which offers up to 103.2 GB of capacity, 
using twenty-four, 4.3 GB disks.  Also being announced today is the 
HA-700W wide shelf for StorageWorks enclosures, offering up to 30GB 
of capacity, using seven, 4.3 GB disks.

     According to Gim Hom, StorageWorks for OEMs product marketing 
manager, "StorageWorks for OEMs offers solutions to satisfy any 
combination of performance, availability and capacity requirements.  
The HA-2400C enclosure, together with the SC-4600 RAID array 
controller, enables OEMs to provide their customers with a high-
performance solution for storing and retrieving critical business 
data."

     David Guy, OEM worldwide sales manager, added, "We designed the  
SC-4600 RAID controller and HA series to be flexible, offering OEMs 
the ability to configure controllers, environmental monitoring 
units, disks, power supplies, and fans for full redundancy."

     The StorageWorks SC-4600 disk array controller provides 
reliable, expandable, cost-effective storage, and sets a new 
performance standard.  With a 32 MB cache and up to 2550 I/O per 
second, the RAID controller is optimized for high-availability 
access to SCSI devices from host computer systems via a Fast Wide 
Differential host interface.

     The SC4600 adaptive cache is used for both reading  and writing  
so that performance can be maximized over the widest range of 
applications.  In dual controller configurations, the SC4600 
features Transparent Failover, a unique host-independent failover 
process.  If one controller fails, the other will automatically take 
over all I/O operations, even adopting the SCSI ID of the failed 
controller so that no host redirection of I/O is required.  Dual 
ported cache also allows outstanding cache write requests to be 
completed even when one controller has failed. 

When housed in the StorageWorks enclosures, such as the new 
HA-2400C, the product offers:

     o	Easy installation, maintenance and expansion with 
        "plug-'n-go" architecture and snap-in components;

     o  Fault tolerance through use of N+1 or redundant disk drives, 
        power supplies, controllers, and fans.

     The HA-2400C enclosure includes 24 building block slots with 
room for a redundant RAID controller, redundant power supplies and 
fans, and a redundant environmental monitoring unit.

     The HA-700W is the first High Availability StorageWorks 
enclosure to support wide, 16- bit SCSI devices in building blocks 
and enables SCSI transfer rates as high as 20 Mbytes per second. The 
HA-700W can be mounted in low-cost pedestal units for standalone 
office installations, or plugged into larger data center enclosures.

Pricing and Availability

     The StorageWorks SC-4600 RAID controller price starts at less 
than $5,000, depending on volume.  The HA-2400C pedestal is priced 
at less than $2,200.  The SC-4600 and HA-2400C are available now.  
The HA-700W will be available in mid-November.  All products are 
sold directly from Digital to qualified OEMs. Call 1-800-333-4545 
for more information.

     Digital's StorageWorks for OEMs Group offers products to OEMs 
ranging from  PC expansion companies to major system manufacturers.  
StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and optical 
storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside, 
departmental, and data center enclosures.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
