            DIGITAL'S NETWORK PRODUCT BUSINESS INTRODUCES
         ITS FIRST RECRUITMENT PROGRAM FOR NETWORK RESELLERS


  Aggressive New Program Will Boost Network Product Business Through 
   Indirect Channels to Over 50 Percent of Network's Revenue In 1995


SAN JOSE, California -- October 17, 1994 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation's Network Product Business today announced a new 
Recruitment Program for network resellers at Tech Decisions '94. 
The new program will give resellers a tremendous opportunity by 
selling Digital's leading-edge networking products such as hubs, 
routers, switches, and network adapter cards.  

     "Resellers are key to driving and growing the Network Product 
Business" according to Jeff Low, vice president of sales and field 
marketing for the Network Product Business.  "In fact, Digital will 
grow the proportion of its worldwide network sales through network 
resellers from 30 percent to over 50 percent during our current 
fiscal year.  We can only do this by investing heavily now in 
helping our existing resellers become more successful and 
aggressively recruiting more of the world's best network resellers.  
This is what the Network Reseller Recruitment Program is all about."

Highlights of Digital's Network Reseller Program include:

     o 	Assigned Local Representative - A Digital accredited 
        reseller can count on personalized attention from a network 
        sales specialist

     o 	Joint sales and marketing seminars and events
     
     o 	Quality lead referrals

     o 	Quarterly marketing programs

     o 	Standard product warranty 

     o 	Network Product Leasing Program 

     o 	A variety of customer support tools

     o 	Training and Support

     According to Lee Cooper, channels development manager for 
Digital's Network Product Business, "This program represents a 
profound change in the Network Product Business sales philosophy as 
it moves from a direct sales model to one focused on indirect 
channels success." 

     Network resellers are increasingly important in the evolving 
'converged' market for hubs, routers, and switches because customers 
must mix and match network components to achieve optimal network 
performance.  "Digital is the best kept secret in networking," said 
Pat Quiqley, a health care sales specialist at Alpha Network 
Technologies in Gaitherburg, MD.  "Once customers understand the
product capabilities of the DEChub 90 and 900, Digital beats the 
competition hands down. Their network sales people are some of the 
best in the industry."

     Frank Mogavero, President of Data Systems West in Woodland 
Hills, CA stated "The Digital sales force is very professional and 
cooperative.  They have taken the time to understand our 
capabilities and bring us into opportunities that match our 
expertise to what customers are looking for."  Ivan Gonzalez, lead 
R&D engineer of Data Systems West added, "The GIGAswitch/FDDI's 
redundancy and performance are unmatched."  

     Digital, as a leading provider of network solutions, continues 
to be a significant contributor to the development of many popular 
networking technologies including Ethernet, FDDI and ATM LANs, 
network switches, routers, bridges, and terminals servers.  Digital 
has networked more than 10 million users worldwide.  For these 
reasons quality network resellers are attracted to the Network 
Product Business Reseller Recruitment Program and to Digital as a 
network partner.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scaleable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
