                  DIGITAL ANNOUNCES ITS FIRST OFFER
         OF FREE PC GRAPHICS SOFTWARE WITH PRINTER PURCHASE


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 18, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today offered purchasers of two of its PC printers from any of 
Digital's commercial distributors a free copy of CorelDRAW Version 3 
or 4 software.  The offer applies to printers purchased between 
September 15, 1994, and March 15, 1995, and are currently available 
from a variety of resellers.  

     "Digital is reinforcing its innovative marketing with this free 
offering of the leading PC graphics software to customers of our PC 
printers," said Larry Cabrinety, Vice President of Digital's 
Components and Peripherals Business Unit. 

     Customers of Digital's color-upgradeable, monochrome ink jet 
DECwriter 500i PC printer will receive a bonus copy of CorelDRAW 3, 
valued at $199.  CorelDRAW 3's drawing power and special effects 
enable users to create vivid desktop publishing documents and 
presentations.  CorelDRAW 3 also includes tools for charting, bitmap 
and photo-editing and presentation as well as over 250 fonts and 
more than 14,000 clip-art images and symbols.

     Purchasers of Digital's color thermal PostScript DECcolorwriter 
1000 PC and Macintosh printer will receive a bonus copy of CorelDRAW 
4, valued at $595.  CorelDRAW 4 expands upon DRAW 3 features by 
providing advanced spreadsheet features, multi-page capabilities, 
over 750 fonts, and more than 18,000 clip-art images and symbols.  
CorelDRAW 4 also includes an additional module, CorelMOVE, which 
lets users combine sound and graphics to produce multimedia 
animations.  Artistic features include over 30,000 variations of 
more than 40 fractal textures imitating natural phenomena such as 
water and marble, and unique "PowerLines" enabling users to draw 
with a variety of customizable shapes.

     "Users will be able to see the difference a high-quality 
printer makes when CorelDRAW graphic designs begin rolling off 
Digital's DECwriter and DECcolorwriter printers," said Dr. Michael 
Cowpland, president and chief executive officer of Corel 
Corporation.  "This combination offers incredible value at a 
reasonable price for end-users throughout North America."

     Customers of either Digital printer will receive a coupon in 
the printer box, which they need to complete and mail along with a 
proof of purchase to Corel Corporation, who will ship the software.  
A choice of media versions is available for each package; either a 
3.5-inch diskette or CD-ROM.  The software requires a minimum of 4 
MBytes of memory on a 386- or 486- CPU with Windows 3.1 or higher.

     The offer applies to end user customers in North America who 
buy the printers (DECwriter 500i, #LJ500-CA, manufacturer's 
suggested list price of $399 or DECcolorwriter 1000, #LF02-CA, 
manufacturer's suggested list price of $4,199) between September 15, 
1994 and March 15, 1995 from VARS who have purchased them from 
Digital's commercial distributors:  Arrow CSG (800-955-9632),
Centauri (800-289-9953), Firstop (800-832-4322), Gates/FA 
(800-332-2222), Hall-Mark (800-884-5675), Ingram Micro 
(800-456-8000), Inland Desktop Express (800-976-1110), Intelligent 
Electronics (800-545-9934), Merisel (800-MERISEL), MicroAge 
(800-887-0045), Pioneer Express (800-227-4712), Pyramid Digital 
(800-416-6600), and TechData (800-237-8931).

     Incorporated in 1985, Corel Corporation is recognized 
internationally as an award-winning developer and marketer of PC 
graphics and SCSI software.  CorelDRAW, Corel's industry-leading 
graphics software, is available in over 17 languages and has won 
over 170 international awards from major trade journals.  Corel 
ships its products through a network of more than 140 distributors 
in 60 countries worldwide.  Corel is traded on the Toronto Stock 
Exchange (symbol: COS) and the NASDAQ -- National Market System 
(symbol: COSFF).

