             DIGITAL INTRODUCES INDUSTRY'S FIRST PRINTER
                  WITH INTERNATIONAL FAX CAPABILITY


  ...Rapidly Expanding Line of Printer Solutions Continues to Offer
                Industry-leading Quality and Price...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 18, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced the DEClaser 3500, a 12 page-per-minute network 
printer that opens users' networks to the world by offering the 
ability to fax and receive PostScript documents domestically and 
internationally directly from the printer.  The DEClaser 3500 
printer is targeted for small to medium-size workgroups who need to 
print and fax professional looking documents quickly and affordably, 
with outstanding resolution, superior reliability, and no loss of 
productivity.

     "Digital's Printer Business is focused on delivering advanced, 
cost-efficient printing solutions that enable companies to work more 
effectively in today's competitive business environment," said Jeb 
Hurley, director of marketing and business operations for Digital's 
Printer Business.  "As our first entry into the multi-function 
printer market, the DEClaser 3500 enables users to fax globally 
right from their desk, saving both time and money, and enhancing the 
quality of printed communications."

     The ability to fax and receive documents directly from the 
PostScript laser printer eliminates the need for PCMCIA fax cards to 
be added to each PC and Macintosh system in the office.
In addition, the high 600 dpi resolution and printing on plain paper 
ensure that documents are easier for recipients to read than 
traditional faxes.  The printer's faxing capability also eliminates 
the time it takes the user to queue to print the document and then 
queue to fax the document.

     The DEClaser 3500 printer provides industry-leading performance 
and output with a 20 MHz RISC processor, 3 MB of memory that is 
expandable to 19 MB, and true Adobe PostScript Level 2.  It also 
includes 53 built-in fonts and an advanced programmable font module.  
Designed to maintain the highest print speed, this optional font 
module enables users to download their favorite fonts, logos, UPC 
codes and barcodes once and then keeps them in memory permanently.

     "The DEClaser 3500 printer is designed for the growing number 
of workgroups that consistently use a variety of applications such 
as business graphics, word processing, desktop publishing and 
spreadsheets," said Robin Tobin, marketing manager for Digital's 
Printer Business.  "The compact size of this printer/fax machine 
makes it optimal for these environments because it fits easily on a 
desktop." 

     As a solution for shared or networked environments, the 
DEClaser 3500 enables complete PC/Windows compatibility right 
out-of-the-box with built-in PCL and PostScript optimized print 
drivers.  Available in models for Macintosh and networked 
environments, the printer features simultaneous active serial, 
bi-directional parallel and LocalTalk ports, as well as TCP/IP, 
NetWare IPX/SPX, Ethertalk, and LAT networking topologies to connect 
to multiple PCs, Macintosh or office systems at the same time. 
The printer has a duty cycle of 20,000 pages per month and will 
hold up to 800 sheets for longer print runs and lower operator 
intervention.  Printer dimensions are 10.5" (H) x 14.4" (W) x 16.0" 
(D).

Pricing and Availability

     Suggested list prices for the DEClaser 3500 printer are $2,099 
for the Macintosh model and $2,199 for the network model.  Both are 
currently available through Digital's worldwide network of 
resellers, distributors and retail partners.  The optional 
PostScript fax capability is available immediately in the U.S. and 
will ship in Holland, Germany and the U.K. within 60 days.  Pricing 
is $349 for the U.S. version.  International pricing will be 
available shortly.  Digital offers a one-year warranty.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
