                DIGITAL'S ALPHA 21164 KEEPS TOP SPOT
             AS COMPETITORS ANNOUNCE NEW MICROPROCESSORS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 18, 1994 --  As competitors announced 
their new RISC (reduced instruction set computing) microprocessors 
at an industry forum, Digital Semiconductor's Alpha 21164 maintained 
its substantial lead in performance and availability.  Announced in 
September, the 21164 running at 300 MHz boasts an estimated 330 
SPECint92 and 500 SPECfp92.  The chip also beat the competition in 
availability, with samples available now and volumes of the 266
MHz version chip shipping in volume in January 1995.  First silicon 
on the chip was achieved in February 1994, again well ahead of the 
competition.

