              DIGITAL ENHANCES COHESIONworX ENVIRONMENT
         WITH NEW TOOL INTEGRATION, X TERMINAL, DCE OPTIONS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 18, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new features of its COHESIONworX software 
development environment that include new, integrated development 
tools, new X terminal and X server support, and optional support of 
the OSF DCE distributed computing environment.

     COHESIONworX is Digital's distributed UNIX software development 
environment that supports computing platforms from Digital, Sun, and 
Hewlett-Packard.  It is the multivendor, client/server foundation 
for Digital's COHESION Team/SEE software engineering and management 
environment.

     "As the industry demands more mature and flexible systems for 
software engineering, Digital continues to improve its COHESIONworX 
product with new tools and support options," said Al Olsen, 
Digital's Software Engineering Marketing group manager.  
"COHESIONworX supports the most popular platforms and operating 
systems, new information access tools, and a  graphical desktop 
interface that is unsurpassed for ease of use."
Tool Integration Support for Data Access

     COHESIONworX V2.1 has added integration of three development 
tools:  WorldView, XRunner, and Mosaic software.  Interleaf 
Corporation's WorldView product is used for viewing and retrieving 
online documentation and for viewing the WorldView Help facility. 
The WorldView product and integration software are packaged with the 
COHESIONworX environment.

     Mercury Interactive Corporation's XRunner tool is used to 
create function and usability tests for graphical user interface 
(GUI) applications.  Integration software is bundled with the 
COHESIONworX product;  the XRunner product is purchased separately 
from Mercury Interactive.

     Mosaic is a distributed, graphical hypermedia tool for 
information browsing, retrieval, and interchange over the global 
Internet.  The COHESIONworX product includes integration software, 
while Mosaic itself is acquired separately.

     COHESIONworX V2.1 also features new support for X terminals 
from Digital and NCD Corporation, as well as for X86 PC-based X 
servers using Hummingbird's eXceed Version 4 PC X server software.

DCE Now Optional

     Digital now offers OSF DCE as an option with COHESIONworX V2.1 
software for large or decentralized development teams that need to 
locate and share information quickly and easily.  With DCE, networks 
of multivendor systems can appear as a single system to the user, to 
speed finding and using data while providing security from 
unauthorized access.  COHESIONworX is also available without the DCE 
option for small and medium-size teams and environments that do not 
require location-independent naming or security capabilities.

     COHESIONworX V2.1 software licenses for DEC OSF/1, SunOS, and 
HP-UX operating systems are priced at $2,300.  Product shipments 
began last week.

Object-Based Software for Transparent Access

     The COHESIONworX Integrated Framework uses Digital's Multi-Cast 
Message Server (MCMS) and ObjectBroker software, Digital's 
implementation of the Object Management Group's CORBA (Common Object 
Request Broker Architecture) specification, to create a virtual 
system on the network. The framework gives engineers transparent 
access to development tools and data residing anywhere on a network 
of systems running the DEC OSF/1, SunOS, or HP-UX operating systems.  
The ability to distribute tool execution across a multivendor 
network preserves a customer's existing investments in software 
tools, hardware, and training.

     The COHESIONworX product includes DEC FUSE code development 
tools and an object-oriented, graphical desktop interface that 
enables developers to build customizable work areas for tools and 
project data.  Support for C, Fortran, and Pascal languages is 
standard;  optional support is also available for COHESIONworX C++ 
and DEC Ada languages.  Support software licenses for C++ and DEC 
Ada programming languages are each priced at $1,000.

     Another option, COHESIONworX EnCASE, provides an open, 
documented toolset that enables developers to add new tools to the 
environment easily and without tool source code modification.  Once 
integrated, a tool can be accessed from the desktop and interact 
with other tools anywhere in the COHESIONworX distributed 
client/server environment.  COHESIONworX EnCASE V2.1 license for DEC 
OSF/1, SunOS, and HP-UX operating systems are priced at $2,400.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
