               DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION ANNOUNCES
                     HEAD OF INVESTOR RELATIONS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 18, 1994 -- Robert E. Hult, 47, has been 
named vice president of Investor Relations at Digital Equipment 
Corporation, Vincent J. Mullarkey, vice president and chief 
financial officer, announced today.

     "Bob brings an extensive knowledge of Digital's business 
operations and the necessary communication and business skills to 
build a strong Investor Relations function for Digital," Mullarkey 
said. "Investor Relations plays a very important role in helping the 
investment community understand our business and the company's plans 
for the future."

     He replaces Bradley Allen, who left the company earlier this 
month to take a position with Cray Research.  

     Hult has held a number of senior financial and operational 
management positions with Digital during his 22 years with the 
company.  Most recently, he was vice president of finance for the 
company's North America and South America operations. He previously 
was vice president of operations for Multivendor Customer Services 
for the Western United States, vice president of finance for 
Asia/Pacific operations, and corporate internal audit director.  
He also has held other key positions in Digital's manufacturing 
and European finance operations.

     Prior to joining Digital, Hult worked for the accounting firm 
of Arthur Andersen in New York.

     Hult holds bachelor and master's degrees in management sciences 
from Rensselaer Polytechnic Institute, an M.B.A. from Babson College 
and attended the executive Program for Management Development at the 
Harvard Business School.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together with 
industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
