    Largest Live On-Line Internet Project Offers Up-to-the-Minute
        Election Results, Comprehensive, Interactive Pre- and
       Post-Election Information for Internet Users Worldwide


SACRAMENTO, Calif. -- October 24, 1994 -- California Acting 
Secretary of State Tony Miller and Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced they are jointly providing the world's first live, 
on-line election results and pre - and post-election information on 
the Internet's World-Wide Web.  Beginning today, users can view 
comprehensive information on the California candidates, ballot 
measures, campaign spending, district maps, and more, in an 
easy-to-read, multimedia format.  On November 8 anyone worldwide 
with Internet access can see California's general election returns 
in graphical, tabular formats, with up-to-the-minute accuracy, 
making this the largest live, on-line Internet project undertaken.  
Following election night, they will be able to access detailed 
summary data on the voting results.  

     To reach the Digital/State of California World-Wide Web server, 
type either http://www.election.digital.com or http://www.election.
ca.gov.  To reach the Gopher server, for textual information and 
flat statistics of live election returns, type gopher.elections.ca.
gov.

     According to Miller, "Such easy and affordable access to 
election information has never before been possible.  I'm extremely 
pleased that with Digital's expertise and equipment, we can provide 
anyone on the Internet a clear view of the candidates and issues 
shaping California's election.  This is a prime example of 
technology aiding the democratic process by providing unedited 
information directly to the public 24 hours a day.  It is also an 
excellent example of how such public-private partnerships can 
benefit citizens."

     "The potential for the Internet's public and commercial use is 
enormous," said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of Digital's 
Internet Business Group.  "The Secretary of State clearly realizes 
the impact this technology can have, and we're pleased to be working 
with his office to implement such a major effort.  By providing a 
powerful, intuitive interface and electronic access to voter and 
election information, Digital is helping the Secretary of State 
deliver on his commitment to make public information easily 
accessible."

     Giordano added that Digital's history of Internet leadership, 
including investing in a significant Internet research effort, 
provided the knowledge needed to quickly design and deliver the 
robust, interactive solution for accessing dynamic on-line 
information.  The company's experiences were gained by being the 
first Fortune 500 company to put a multimedia server on the 
World-Wide Web, the first computer vendor to enable customers to 
test-drive products over the Internet, and the first to install an 
interactive "village," e.g., the Citizens' Network for the City of 
Palo Alto.

Delivering the Internet/Election System

     To help the Secretary of State deliver the California election 
services, Digital's Palo Alto, Calif. research facility is "hosting" 
the system with a World-Wide Web server providing information in an 
interactive, multimedia environment.  It is also providing a Gopher 
Server that shows live election returns in a hierarchical text 
format.

     Digital is providing a full range of systems integration 
services and powerful products to the Secretary of State, to 
facilitate the Internet/California State Election program: 
        
     o	Management and design of the network infrastructure, 
        including an extremely high bandwidth for high-volume user 
        access to the system 

     o	World-Wide Web multimedia data preparation and presentation, 
        putting the election information in easy-to-understand, 
        interesting graphical formats for users worldwide 

     o	Hypertext access links within the California Election Web 
        Server and to/from other World-Wide Web servers, enabling 
        users to search and browse through information sources, as 
        their interests dictate 

     o	Alpha AXP 2100 servers, which provide the high performance 
        and capacity needed to handle high-volume public access of 
        dynamic information 
     
     o	Statistical data summarizing usage, and indicating general 
     	interests, resulting from access of the World-Wide Web 
        server


Internet/California Election System Content

     California Secretary of State staff and members of Digital's 
Internet Business Group and California-based research labs, are 
together delivering the California Election/Internet system.  In 
addition to live, on-line election night returns, there is a wealth 
of information now available on the Web server, which will be 
updated constantly with content on the races, candidates and 
campaign finances.  

Now available: 

     o	Entire contents of the official California Voter Information 
     	Pamphlet published by the Secretary of State's office, e.g., 
        state-wide candidates, ballot propositions (full text and 
        nonpartisan analysis), political party goals, and electoral 
        procedures

     o	Interactive map of California counties, which will provide 
        return information by county when clicked on during the 
        elections
     
     o	Photographs of state-wide candidates

     o	Links to other voting information

     Post-election information will include final election results, 
access statistics and general feedback from accessors.  (Note: the 
feedback will not be attributed to any individual.)

     This is the second, and most extensive, public information 
Internet initiative conducted by California.  The first, the State's 
text-based Gopher Server, was used in a pilot project accessed by 
400,000 Internet users for information on the primary election in 
June, 1994.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
