          S.W.I.F.T. INTERFACE APPLICATIONS TO BE AVAILABLE
                     ON DIGITAL'S ALPHA SYSTEMS


BOSTON, Mass. -- October 24, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and S.W.I.F.T. today announced the port of S.W.I.F.T. interface 
applications - SWIFTAlliance and ST400 - to Digital's Alpha  
platform.  Moving SWIFTAlliance and ST400 to Alpha will allow 
S.W.I.F.T. users to take advantage of the outstanding price/
performance leadership offered by Alpha systems.  SWIFTAlliance 
will be released under the DEC OSF/1 operating system, Digital's 
implementation of the UNIX operating system.  Porting is underway 
with general customer availability planned for mid 1995.

     "We are delighted about the progress we made in the past few 
months and the continuing alliance between S.W.I.F.T. and Digital," 
said Marion Dancy, manager of Digital's Financial Services group.  
"During SIBOS '93,  S.W.I.F.T. announced SWIFTAlliance as an open-
systems based interface to the S.W.I.F.T. system.  This demonstrates 
Digital's continued commitment to make the industries premier 
applications available on the Alpha platform."

     "Ivo Demeersman, SWIFTAlliance project manager stated, "DEC 
OSF/1 has proven conformance to the defined standards. During the 
initial development of SWIFTAlliance we have followed strict 
programming standards and are very pleased with the ease of porting 
our application to the Alpha platform." 

     Digital and S.W.I.F.T. also announced that S.W.I.F.T.'s 
successful ST400 interface is being made available on Alpha systems 
running the OpenVMS operating system.  General customer availability 
is scheduled for the end of 1995.  S.W.I.F.T. ST400 product manager 
Alastair Chisholm said "Alpha is a natural evolution for all our 
ST400 customer base and new high-volume users."

     The SWIFTAlliance application is being shown running on Alpha 
systems at SIBOS '94, in Boston, Massachusetts, October 24-28.  
Since ST400 on Alpha and SWIFTAlliance use the same platform, ST400 
users on Alpha who anticipate moving to SWIFTAlliance in the future 
will protect the major part of their hardware investment. 

     The Alpha family is an extensive range of fully compatible 
64-bit systems, from desktop to data center.  Adding Alpha to the 
range of platforms supporting interface applications will make it 
possible to satisfy performance requirements for a wide range of 
users interfacing to the S.W.I.F.T. network. 

     S.W.I.F.T. supports the data communication and processing needs 
of financial institutions in payments, forex and money markets, 
securities and trade finance.  Its dedicated network connects more 
than 4,400 financial institutions in 115 countries and provides 
non-stop, rapid, secure and cost-effective communications.  In 
addition to financial message processing, services include bulk data 
transfer, support for real-time gross settlement in large-value 
national payment systems, and forex confirmation matching and 
netting for financial institutions. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
