                     DIGITAL UNVEILS AGGRESSIVE
                        ADVERTISING CAMPAIGN


           New Campaign Drives Worldwide Branding Program


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 25, 1994 -- As part of its continuing 
effort to strengthen its global image and provide a singular 
corporate voice, Digital Equipment Corporation today launched a new, 
comprehensive marketing and advertising campaign.  The campaign 
centers on the company's core product and technology strengths, with 
heavy emphasis on customer benefits.  The heart of the campaign 
focuses on Digital's adoption of a mission critical attitude to do 
whatever it takes toward becoming more competitive in today's 
marketplace, in turn making customers more competitive. 

    "With this campaign, Digital is approaching the market with a 
clear identity that will differentiate us from the competition," 
stated Charlie Holleran, vice president, communications.  "In the 
past, the great majority of Digital's marketing messages were very 
technical in nature.  This campaign enables us to communicate the 
value of our products and services to our customers in a clear, 
direct, and concise manner."

    "This new campaign will form the foundation for developing a 
strategic platform to position Digital, while establishing a 
differentiated, clear, strong, and competitive brand," said Janet 
Shipman, director, worldwide brand communications.  "This 
non-conformist, cut-through-the-clutter campaign truly depicts a 
rejuvenated Digital."

    DDB Needham Worldwide, Digital's agency, has created a series of 
hard-hitting, aggressive print and television ads that drives home 
the two key attributes of "the new Digital:" that the company and 
its people will do whatever it takes to make customers more 
competitive, and that the Digital difference will be a "mission-
critical" attitude and behavior. The ads, which debut in the global 
edition of the Wall Street Journal, target three main audiences: key 
decision makers, or "vetoers;" "intelligent recommenders," who deal 
with technically sophisticated issues; and "consumers," generally 
end users and department heads who often are not as interested in 
technical detail, but who are interested in buying a brand they can 
trust and rely on.  

    Digital's lead, strategic creative partner, DDB Needham 
Worldwide, will spearhead the integration of the key campaign 
messages into additional marketing communications programs.  These 
include events marketing, direct marketing, promotional materials 
development, and sales promotion, as well as programs for resellers 
and retail markets.  

    As one key element of Digital's integrated, global 
communications strategy, this campaign marks a renewed commitment 
toward achieving marketing excellence for the corporation," 
concluded Holleran.        

    Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace. 
