               DIGITAL EXTENDS STORAGE LEADERSHIP WITH
            NEW OFFERINGS FOR ALPHA AXP AND VAX PLATFORMS


            New Array Controller, Write-Back Cache, RAID,
           Storage Management, Tape and Optical Solutions
               for OpenVMS and OSF/1 Operating Systems


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 25, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today introduced a new range of storage solutions that further 
extends its leadership in providing data storage for Alpha AXP and 
VAX computing platforms.  Included in today's announcement are a new 
DSSI Array Controller, RAID and Write-Back Cache options for 
StorageWorks subsystems, new storage management software products, 
tape drive and tape library storage solutions and additional optical 
storage families.

     "Today's announcements demonstrate Digital's commitment to 
delivering a full range of proven storage solutions to the OpenVMS 
and Alpha AXP computing environments," said Bob Condon, Digital's 
marketing manager for storage on Digital platforms.  "This range of 
new hardware and software products and enhancements enables Digital 
to provide customers with cost-effective storage solutions tailored 
to their evolving capacity, data availability and performance 
needs."

DSSI Array Controller

     The HSD30 Array Controller, a new addition to the DSSI 
subsystems solutions line-up, provides connection for up to twenty-
one storage devices on a single DSSI port, with RAID 0 (striping) 
on-board.  Optionally, up to 32MB of read cache and dual-redundant 
controller capability with failover is provided.

     The new RAID and Write-back Cache options described below also 
are supported by this new controller, the HSD30.

Write-Back Cache

     Up to 32MB of array controller cache can now be deployed for 
write operations as well as read caching via the non-volatile 
Write-Back Cache feature.  This allows applications to continue 
working rather than wait until write requests are completed to disk.  
The Write-Back Cache option is supported on the HSJ-series, the 
HSZ40 and the new HSD30 array controllers.

RAID

     Digital's new RAID (Redundant Array of Independent Disks) 
offerings are designed to enable a full range of availability and 
performance options across multiple application environments:


     o  The Array Controller Raid option, supported on HSJ-series, 
        HSZ40 and the new HSD30 controllers, provides a data 
        availability solution approaching that of shadowing or 
        mirroring at a fraction of the cost.  Digital's innovative 
        RAID implementation dynamically adjusts to maximize 
        performance for both throughput intensive (RAID 5) and 
        bandwidth intensive (RAID 3) applications.  In combination 
        with the new Write-Back Cache option, RAID performance is 
        increased to a level normally associated with striping and 
        with much higher data availability than is characteristic of 
        striping.

     o  The SW300 StorageWorks RAID Office Expansion Pedestal for 
        CI, DSSI and SCSI-based systems allows configuration of up 
        to twenty-four 3.5" disks, two controllers, two cache 
        accelerator modules and eight power supplies; or eight 5.25" 
        disks, or mixed combinations.

     o  RAID Software for OpenVMS systems provides software-based 
        striping (RAID 0), RAID 5 capabilities (striping and 
        parity), and disk partitioning, providing the benefits of 
        RAID technology without the purchase of additional hardware.
     	Customers who currently use striping on OpenVMS VAX systems 
        can upgrade to Raid Software for OpenVMS via a special 
        discount offer (see separate fact sheet for details).

Storage Management Software Tools

     According to Ed McCarren, Digital's storage software marketing 
manager, "Digital's new suite of storage management tools is 
designed to increase dramatically the productivity of systems 
managers and their end users.  By providing robust storage 
management solutions of proven reliability, we can offer our 
customers cost-effective answers to their data storage and retrieval 
needs."

     To help Digital platform customers efficiently and cost-
effectively leverage their various storage investments, Digital's 
Storage Business Unit is providing these new storage management 
software tools:
   
     o  Hierarchical Storage Management for OpenVMS V1.0 is a 
        layered software product that extends the OpenVMS file 
        system, allowing efficient management of infrequently 
        accessed data by increasing data availability and user
     	productivity while reducing backup time.
   
     o  Save Set Manager for OpenVMS V1.0 is a layered software 
        product that can dramatically reduce operational time during 
        OpenVMS backup activities by providing offline save set 
        validation, copy and merge functions.   

     o  Desktop Backup/Archiver V2.0, a next-generation 
        client/server backup management tool for OpenVMS-based 
        Pathworks LANS, provides easy-to-use backup, restore and 
        archive capabilities.  It protects existing investments by 
        backup of local storage on PCs or MacIntosh computers to an 
        OpenVMS VAX or Alpha AXP server.

     o  Optical Storage Management Software V3.2 facilitates easy 
        sharing of the optical storage jukebox within an OpenVMS 
        environment, simplifying application access to vast 
        quantities of low-cost, near-on-line storage.

     o  Networker Save and Restore Software V3.0 is Digital's 
        proven, reliable data protection product for TCP-IP 
        heterogeneous networks.  New with V3.0 are media pools, a 
        powerful tool for the management of growing media libraries.  
        NSR supports up to 20 UNIX(tm) and PC platforms backed up to 
        OSF servers.

     o  Storage Library System (SLS) V2.4 for OpenVMS VAX and AXP 
        platforms is Digital's solution for managing the backup and 
        archiving of critical corporate data.  SLS is a layered 
        software product designed to manage collections of removable 
        media and the devices associated with saving and retrieving 
        data stored on the media.  It also provides for the easy 
        automation of backup tasks.

Tape and Optical

     Digital is extending its breadth of tape and optical solutions 
for the OpenVMS VAX and Alpha AXP environments with new subsystems 
and device support:

     o  The TLZ07 tape drive represents the next generation of 4mm 
        DAT and provides up to 8GB of unattended backup and 
        archiving capabilities, with transfer rates of up to 
        810KB/second. 

     o  The TL820 DLT tape library is Digital's newest member of 
        near-on-line automated storage library products, providing 
        up to 5.2 Tbytes of storage for unattended backup 
        operations, archiving, large-scale data storage, and most 
        recently for video-on-demand applications.

     o  RV700 family of write-once, read many (WORM) optical storage 
        jukeboxes comprises scalable 12" media products that meet 
        customer requirements for cost-effective, reliable, large 
        scale automated data and image storage.

     o  The RW500 family of optical storage jukeboxes, ranging from 
        19GB to 170GB in formatted capacity in multifunctional 
        optical storage drives, now is available at cost savings of 
        as much as 17% from earlier pricing.  This proven jukebox 
        family is designed to provide quick, automated access to 
        large quantities of data at a cost lower than either on-line 
        or operator-attended off-line storage.  Optical storage is 
        extremely stable media with a shelf life of up to 30 years, 
        and is less susceptible to environmental changes than most 
        other media.

     According to McCarren, "We are excited about our new devices 
and our comprehensive and growing family of storage management 
products.  By combining efficient, high-capacity hardware with 
powerful, robust storage management software, we provide our 
customers with complete unattended backup and storage management 
solutions from the desktop to the full enterprise."

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable, desktop, deskside and 
data-center enclosures.  StorageWorks products are available on 
multiple operating systems and hardware platforms, including 
Digital's Alpha AXP and VAX systems, Novell environments, and Sun 
Microsystems workstations. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.
