              DIGITAL INTRODUCES INDUSTRY'S LOWEST COST
                        COLOR INK JET PRINTER


               Aggressively Challenges Hewlett-Packard


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 26, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today introduced the industry's lowest cost color ink jet printer, 
the DECcolorwriter 120ic printer.  The DECcolorwriter 120ic printer 
boasts a list price 14% below Hewlett-Packard's competitive offering 
and provides color "Write Out-of-the-Box," so users do not have to 
purchase a separate color kit.  Digital also announced the DECwriter 
110i printer, the lowest cost ink jet printer that offers the option 
to upgrade to color.  Both printers feature the speed and quality 
needed for home and small office use. 

      "As part of Digital's mission-critical attitude, we are 
committed to being a more aggressive player in the highly 
competitive printer market," said Larry Cabrinety, Vice President of 
Digital's Components & Peripherals Business Unit. "Today's 
announcement expands our family of affordably-priced, industry-
leading personal desktop printers that increase productivity by 
enabling users to print wherever they work." 

     "Digital's DECcolorwriter 120ic printer is ideal for our 
retail partners," said Patrick Sullivan, vice president, Digital
Merchandising Group for Components & Peripherals Business Unit.
"It meets their critical margin and quantity requirements, as well 
as the cost and output needs of their customers. With products like 
the DECcolorwriter 120ic printer, Digital continues to underscore 
the competitiveness of its printer offerings to the industry." 

DECcolorwriter 120ic/DECwriter 110i

     Featuring color "Write Out-of-the-Box," the DECcolorwriter 
120ic printer offers the industry's lowest cost for a high-quality, 
color PC printer.  The printer provides a print speed of up to 3
pages-per-minute, laser-like resolution, seven resident fonts, a
duty-cycle of up to 600 pages-per-month, and a replaceable ink
cartridge that enables users to save 43% over competing products on 
the cost of monochrome ink.  A user-friendly printer, the
DECcolorwriter 120ic printer also has an ink low/out indicator, an 
automatic 70-page integrated sheet feeder or the option for manual 
feed, support for printing on letter, A4, legal, labels, envelopes 
and transparencies, and easy to read documentation for quick 
installation.  In addition, the printer includes a 128Kb input 
buffer that increases productivity by enabling users to get back to 
work faster, a Windows 3.1 printer driver, standard parallel 
interface, PCL 3 emulation, and is Energy Star compliant. 

     For home and small office users who want mostly monochrome 
printing with the option to upgrade to color, Digital's new 
DECwriter 110i printer is the lowest cost color-capable ink jet 
printer available.  With the exception of this color option, the 
DECwriter 110i printer offers the same industry leading features 
as the DECcolorwriter 120ic printer. 

Pricing and Availability

     Suggested list price for the DECcolorwriter 120ic printer is 
$355.  List price for the DECwriter 110i printer is $319, with the 
color option priced at $44.  The DECcolorwriter 120ic printer will 
be sold through Digital's retail channels in the U.S., including 
Circuit City, CompUSA, Fry, Lechmere, Sun TV, and more.  The 
DECwriter 110i printer and color option will be available through 
Digital's U.S. distributors, including Arrow SCG, Centauri, Firstop, 
Gates/FA, Hall-Mark, Ingram Micro, Inland Desktop Express, 
Intelligent Electronics, Merisel, MicroAge, Pioneer Express, Pyramid 
Digital, and TechData.  All the printers are offered with a two year 
warranty.  Information is available by calling Digital at 
1-800-777-4343. 

