         DIGITAL ANNOUNCES VENTURIS LINE OF DESKTOP SYSTEMS


        Low-Cost Business PCs with Advanced Functionality for
                     Increased User Productivity


MAYNARD, Mass. -- October 31, 1994 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced its new, entry-level Venturis line -- a family of 
eight affordable, desktop Pentium and 486 systems. The Venturis 
line replaces Digital's popular DECpc LPv+ and DECpc LPx+ Value 
Line.

     The aggressively-priced Venturis line, with models starting as 
low as $1,079, is aimed at the volume purchaser in medium and large 
organizations. Easy to deploy, install and maintain, the new PCs 
are designed to meet the performance requirements of general 
business users as well as those of users in client/server 
environments. The Venturis line provides an optimum balance of 
graphics, disk subsystems and processors for basic office 
applications such as word processing, transaction processing, 
e-mail, and communications.

     The Venturis announcement is the second in a series of major 
new product announcements this fall from Digital's Personal Computer 
Business Unit. Like the recently-introduced Celebris line, the 
Venturis line features a new naming convention, new packaging, new 
enclosures and a new start-up menu, and helps PC users become more 
productive, more quickly.

     "With the introduction of the Venturis line, Digital again 
moves beyond offering just excellent engineering and technology, to 
focusing more on how people can better interact with their computers 
-- from the new 'Getting Started' menus and 'Quick Set-Up Guide' to 
the uniquely-designed easy-access enclosures," said Bernhard Auer, 
vice president and general manager of Digital's PC Business Unit.

Superior Capabilities with Solid Performance

     "With Venturis systems, Digital continues its tradition of 
providing PC users with leading-edge technology, excellent price/
performance and ease-of-use," said Howard Elias, vice president, 
Desktop Product Line.

The new Venturis systems:

     o	incorporate Plug and Play capabilities that enable faster 
        upgrades and more reliable system performance;

     o	ensure Windows 95 compatibility, enabling PCs to take 
        advantage of the new version of Microsoft Windows;

     o	use S3's Trio32, Trio64 and Vision864 graphics accelerators 
        for improved graphics performance;

     o	include Desktop Management Interface (DMI) capabilities for 
        more efficient distributed computing;

     o	implement Advanced Power Management and Energy Star 
        compliance across the line, including the Pentium 60, for 
        energy-efficient computing;

     o	incorporate multiple levels of security that prevent 
        unauthorized use and access to desktop information; and

     o	offer multimedia, office and networking options, which 
        enable customers to expand the capabilities of PCs as their 
        computing needs evolve.

Ease-of-Use Initiatives

     All Venturis models provide easy access to product and service 
information to assist system administrators and resellers in getting 
users up and running. The 'Getting Started' screen includes system 
specific introductory information, help screens, user registration 
and service and support information. The Venturis 'Quick Setup 
Guide' has illustrated installation instructions. User assistance 
for system functions, such as network setup, advanced power 
management settings, plug and play ISA configuration, and resource 
configuration is also included.

     Also designed for ease-of-maintenance, all Venturis models 
include features such as a latched enclosure that allows easy access 
to the system. The swivel sub-assembly enables easy installation of 
hard drives. In addition, easy access to the motherboard 
accommodates upgrades and service.

     Digital's entire Venturis family, including the Pentium 60 
model, complies with the U.S. government's Energy Star power 
conservation guideline, making Digital's PCs 'easy' on the 
environment, as well as offering energy saving value for customers.

     Each system features multi-levels of security features, 
including an external chassis keylock, keyboard and mouse password, 
diskette access control, hard drive access control and multiple-
level password protection. The new Venturis PCs come with Digital's 
worldwide service and support through a limited three-year warranty, 
including one year on site.

Desktop Management Interface (DMI) Ready

     DMI functions will enable network administrators to manage PCs on
networks for enhanced communications and more efficient distributed
computing. Digital's Venturis family is DMI ready, which will provide 
significant advancements in network administration of an organization's
client/server computing environment. Venturis DMI will allow desktop
client hardware and software status reporting, asset management across
a network, remote diagnostics of client PCs, and improved management of
a company's enterprise-wide, distributed computing environment. 

     Five of the eight new Digital Venturis systems -- the Digital 
Venturis 433sx, 450s2, 466, 4100 and 560 -- offer slimline 
enclosures. The full profile Digital Venturis FP450s2, FP466 and 
FP4100 feature a five slot and five bay enclosure. U.S. list prices 
range from $1,079 for the Digital Venturis 433sx to $1,899 for the 
Digital Venturis FP4100. All models are available now.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha AXP 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete in today's global marketplace.
